(also see 'help class')

~
0 KILLER THIEF~
(KILLER) flags are a marker that show someone was aggressive towards
another player. This will cause guards and protectors to be aggressive
towards them.

(THIEF) flags are a marker that someone tried to steal something from
someone and failed to do so. Anyone with this flag alone will receive a
(KILLER) when attacked.

To remove one of these flags you must die to another player other than a
fellow clan mate. In odd situations an immortal may pardon this flag, as
long as there is a very good reason.

~
1 RACE REMORTS REMORTING 'RACE REMORT'~
Syntax: remort <sub-race>

Once you reach level 51 you can remort your character and pick a new
sub-race which will provide you with new skills and spells, but also
new limitations.
In order to remort you must have a certain number of quest points.  To
see the number of QP you need type "remort".
Remorting removes all the equipment you are wearing and puts it in your
inventory.  It sets the character back to level 1 and puts you at
(20hp 100mana 50mv).  All your old and new skills/spells get set back
to 1% (except weapon that gets set to 40%).  You automatically get the
main weapon for your class type.  Your hours are put back to 0, wimpy
is set to 0, and you are given 3 trains and 5 practices.  You get to keep
your clan affiliation and can be pkilled at level 1.  If you have a killer
or thief flag at the time, it will be removed.  Also any skills or spells
your mort gained after creation gets added to the remorts CP.
The sub-races you can choose from include:
Red Dragon: Ruby or Fire
Blue Dragon: Sapphire or Sky
Green Dragon: Emerald or Malachite
White Dragon: Pearl or Mist
Black Dragon: Onyx or Shadow
Elves: Forest or Drow
Dwarves: Mountain or Grey
Giant: Hill or Cave
Human: Doppleganger or Medusa
Troll: Two-Headed or Spectral
Sliver: Stinging or Abyssal
Gargoyle: Sentinel or Haunting
Kirre: Dark or Sabre
Marid: Nereid or Befouler

(see also help <sub-class>, help 'first remort') 

~
1 RUBY RED DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.
Ruby dragons are known to be wise and regal, but also snobbish.  They are  
proud of their skill to "thrust" an extra attack if successful at parry.   
They also have the spell "loneliness" which can be cast on an opponent to  
make the where command useless.  

~
1 FIRE RED DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
Fire dragons are greedy, vain, and confident.  They have an extra attack   
skill that allows them to "dragon bite" their opponents if dodge is  
successful.  They also have the ability to lower their armor class by 
casting the spell of "scalemail".  

~
1 SAPPHIRE BLUE DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
Sapphire dragons are usually peaceful and not militant.  They can avoid  
fights by casting "cone of fear" which forces their enemy to flee.  They  
also have gained a "gemology" skill, which allows them to convert gems   
into throwing objects.  

~
1 SKY BLUE DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
Sky dragons are very unpredictable and could do anything while in combat.  
They can cast "lightning spear" which will connect with an opponent a few  
rooms away.  They have also gained "presence" which informs them if an  
enemy enters their area.  

~
1 EMERALD GREEN DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
Emerald dragons are known to be curious and paranoid.  Their main protective 
weapon is their "wail" spell which can deafen their enemy giving them -saves 
and -dex and causes a little damage. They also have the spell "loneliness"  
which can be cast on an opponent to make his where skill useless.  

~
1 MALACHITE GREEN DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Malachite dragons are level-headed and calculating. They can cast 'drakor'
to shift a target's alignment toward evil, and can call down 'acid rain' on
their foes, drenching the room in corrosive precipitation.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  drakor      - Shifts a target's alignment toward evil
  acid rain   - Drenches the room in corrosive acid

~
0 'ACID RAIN'~
Syntax: cast 'acid rain'

Malachite dragons can call down a torrent of corrosive acid upon the area,
drenching everyone in the room each round with burning precipitation. The
acid eats into flesh and can corrode equipment on those it strikes.

Acid rain only works outdoors and cannot be cast inside buildings or
enclosed spaces. The rain persists until it dissipates naturally.

This spell is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Malachite Dragon (remort only)

~
1 PEARL WHITE DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.  
{x
Pearl dragons are known to be friendly and charming.  They have gained  
"presence" which informs them if an enemy enters their area. They also have  
the skill "shed" that allows them to pluck their scales off and use them as  
throwing objects.Additionally they can cast an "aurora" on themselves which
significantly increases their mana regeneration for a short time.

~
1 MIST WHITE DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
{x
Mist dragons are known to be solitary and philosophical.  Their learned ways 
has provided them with a "melior" spell which can turn a mob or characters  
alignment to good.  They also have the ability to cast "discordance" and  
turn a group of attacking charmies against the owner. Additionally they
can cloak themselves and allies in "misty cloak" which makes them harder
to hit.

~
1 ONYX BLACK DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
Onyx dragons are known for selfish, erratic, and unfriendly behavior.    
They have gained a protective "cloud of poison" spell, that cloaks them and  
poisons an attacker for each successful hit.  They also have attained a  
"retreat" skill, which halts a fight and makes it look like they have fled  
the room.  

~
1 SHADOW BLACK DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates.   
Shadow dragons are sly, devious, and not known risk takers.  They have the  
ability to "create shadow" which summons a charmie with the same name and  
short description as the dragon. All shadow dragons have learned to conceal    
themselves with the hide skill as well, especially at night.

~
1 DROW ELF REMORT~
All elven remorts have superior control of their surroundings. They gain
the "reflection" ability, which throws back damage spells to the caster.
This heightened self-reliance makes them unwilling to group with anyone
more than 250 alignment points away from themselves.

Drow elves are aggressive fighters who can cast "primal rage" upon
themselves, granting a level-based bonus to hit and damage. Their time
spent deep underground has enhanced their infravision into true dark
vision, allowing them to see clearly even in complete darkness.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All elf remorts:  reflection
  Drow Elf:         primal rage, dark vision (permanent)

~
1 FOREST ELF REMORT~
All elven remorts have superior control of their surroundings. They gain
the "reflection" ability, which throws back damage spells to the caster.
This heightened self-reliance makes them unwilling to group with anyone
more than 250 alignment points away from themselves.

Forest elves are in tune with the natural world. They have mastered the
art of mixing ingredients to "brew" four different potions.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All elf remorts:  reflection
  Forest Elf:       brew

~
1 MOUNTAIN DWARF REMORT~
All dwarven remorts have trained harder than most and gained the "wild
swing" skill, which lets them strike multiple opponents in a single blow.
Their time spent in the deep mines has expanded their infravision into
true dark vision, allowing them to see clearly in complete darkness.

Mountain dwarves have spent their lives in pursuit of gold, making them
greedy and resourceful. They have acquired the "conversion" skill, which
allows them to melt down equipment and convert it to gold. Many mountain
dwarves have also turned to drink  -  a lifestyle that has sharpened their
fighting instincts. When drunk, mountain dwarves deal bonus damage in
combat, a style known as "drunken master."
Skills/Spells gained:
  All dwarf remorts:  wild swing, dark vision (permanent)
  Mountain Dwarf:     conversion, drunken master (passive bonus when drunk)

~
1 GREY DWARF REMORT~
All dwarven remorts have trained harder than most and gained the "wild
swing" skill, which lets them strike multiple opponents in a single blow.
Their time spent in the deep mines has expanded their infravision into
true dark vision, allowing them to see clearly in complete darkness.

Grey dwarves are malicious and hostile. They can use "turn magic" to seize
control of charmies summoned by other characters. They also protect
themselves with "enlargement," which temporarily increases their saves and
hit points at the cost of dexterity.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All dwarf remorts:  wild swing, dark vision (permanent)
  Grey Dwarf:         turn magic, enlargement

~
1 HILL GIANT REMORT~
All giant remorts gain great surges in strength. They sometimes have the
ability to "behead" opponents outright, and their throwing arm allows them
to "carve boulders" from the ground in forests, fields, hills, mountains,
and deserts. Giant remorts are too aggressive to flee  -  wimpy is disabled.

Hill giants are brutish guardians who can "block exit" to prevent others
from leaving a room. They also know the "robustness" spell, which
temporarily raises their maximum hit points.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All giant remorts:  beheading, carve boulder
  Hill Giant:         block exit, robustness

~
1 CAVE GIANT REMORT~
All giant remorts gain great surges in strength. They sometimes have the
ability to "behead" opponents outright, and their throwing arm allows them
to "carve boulders" from the ground in forests, fields, hills, mountains,
and deserts. Giant remorts are too aggressive to flee  -  wimpy is disabled.

Cave giants have grey, rock-like skin and have learned to tame wild bears
as guards. The "cave bears" spell summons 1-4 bears for protection, but
cannot be used while the giant already has charmies. They also receive the
ability to wear "animal skins," allowing them to protect themselves with
thick animal hides.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All giant remorts:  beheading, carve boulder
  Cave Giant:         cave bears, animal skins

~
1 DOPPLEGANGER HUMAN REMORT~
All human remorts have mutated into new forms. The strain of transformation
greatly increases their hunger and thirst, causing them to require food and
water twice as fast as normal. All human remorts also gain the permanent
ability to walk on water.

Dopplegangers gain the "shapeshift" skill, which changes their short
description to that of a mob in the same room. They can only hold this
form for a limited time, and revert to their original form if attacked.
Dopplegangers are also resistant to charm.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All human remorts:  water walk (permanent)
  Doppleganger:       shapeshift, charm resistance

~
1 MEDUSA HUMAN REMORT~
All human remorts have mutated into new forms. The strain of transformation
greatly increases their hunger and thirst, causing them to require food and
water twice as fast as normal. All human remorts also gain the permanent
ability to walk on water.

Medusas gain the "snake bite" skill, which does minor damage but poisons
the victim and acts as a possible 3rd or 4th attack. They also gain
"granite stare," a spell which turns a single mob to stone  -  the mob
crumbles to dust along with any equipment and gold on it. Medusas are
also resistant to poison.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All human remorts:  water walk (permanent)
  Medusa:             snake bite, granite stare, poison resistance

~
1 SPECTRAL TROLL REMORT~
All troll remorts gain an improved regeneration system. If hit hard enough
in combat, body parts may be cleaved off, but the "regrowth" ability allows
them to reattach quickly. However, they have developed a weakness to
sunlight and take damage when outdoors during noontime hours.

Spectral trolls are permanently invisible, fading in and out of existence
like wraiths. They are also permanently "ocularied"  -  a state that marks
them as perceptible to others with detect invisibility even while unseen.
They can call spirits from another plane to act as "familiar" guards that
announce all who pass by. Their ghostly presence lets them inflict "fear"
on victims, limiting their ability to deal damage.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All troll remorts:  regrowth
  Spectral Troll:     familiar, fear, permanent invisibility, permanent oculary

~
1 TWO-HEADED TWOHEADED TROLL REMORT~
All troll remorts gain an improved regeneration system. If hit hard enough
in combat, body parts may be cleaved off, but the "regrowth" ability allows
them to reattach quickly. However, they have developed a weakness to
sunlight and take damage when outdoors during noontime hours.

Two-headed trolls have grown an extra head, allowing them to wear an
additional piece of headgear and "speak" through it, acting like the say
channel. These trolls can also "bite" opponents in combat, with troll bites
known to cause the plague.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All troll remorts:   regrowth
  Two-Headed Troll:    bite, speak (second head slot, acts as say channel)

~
1 STINGING SLIVER REMORT~
All sliver remorts gain a deeper connection to their magical powers. They
keep their own sliver ability (e.g. a Vorlath Sliver retains its mana bonus
for itself). They also gain "telepathy," alerting them whenever another
sliver enters the realm. However, rain makes them sluggish  -  water
collecting on their frames weakens them.

Stinging slivers can weave a "web" across a room to ensnare prey. They can
also use "corpse drain" to suck nutrients from a slain enemy, restoring
their own health.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All sliver remorts:   telepathy
  Stinging Sliver:      web, corpse drain

~
1 ABYSSAL SLIVER REMORT~
All sliver remorts gain a deeper connection to their magical powers. They
keep their own sliver ability (e.g. a Vorlath Sliver retains its mana bonus
for itself). They also gain "telepathy," alerting them whenever another
sliver enters the realm. However, rain makes them sluggish  -  water
collecting on their frames weakens them.

Abyssal slivers command powerful storms. Non-clanners gain "hailstorm,"
which strikes mobs only; clanners instead gain "rain of tears," which
strikes both mobs and clanners in the room.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All sliver remorts:  telepathy
  Abyssal Sliver:      hailstorm or rain of tears (based on clan status)

~
1 SENTINEL GARGOYLE REMORT~
All gargoyle remorts deepen their protective abilities. They gain "mass
protect," bestowing powerful protective magic upon themselves. They also
learn "stone sleep," which accelerates healing while sleeping  -  though
stone sleep does force gargoyles to sleep in order to trigger healing.

Sentinel gargoyles are protective and combat-oriented. Their horns grow
long enough to "gore" opponents. They can also create a "homonculus" to
fight alongside them.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All gargoyle remorts:  stone sleep, mass protect
  Sentinel Gargoyle:     gore, homonculus

~
1 HAUNTING GARGOYLE REMORT~
All gargoyle remorts deepen their protective abilities. They gain "mass
protect," bestowing powerful protective magic upon themselves. They also
learn "stone sleep," which accelerates healing while sleeping  -  though
stone sleep does force gargoyles to sleep in order to trigger healing.

Haunting gargoyles are eerie and unsettling. They can emit a "shriek" that
deals damage to all who hear it. They can also "displace" themselves,
teleporting by switching places with another being in the area.

Skills/Spells gained:
  All gargoyle remorts:   stone sleep, mass protect
  Haunting Gargoyle:      shriek, displace

~
1 FIRST REMORT SKILLS SPELLS 'FIRST REMORT'~
All classes, upon remorting, gain the following skills:
Throw             Taste             Butcher             Recall            Rub
Magic-users (mages, conjurers, enchanters, invokers) also gain:
Detonation        Mutate            Call to Arms        Confusion         Weaponsmith
Religious classes (druids, clerics) also gain:
