55 AFFECT AFFECTS IMM~
Syntax: affect <character>
Syntax: affect <character> remove <affect>

This command when used with just a character name will list all the affects
on that character.  When the 'remove' keyword is added, you can remove one
affect from a character.  Consider it a more refined version of 'blank'.
You do not need to be in the same room as your target.
See also BLANK.

~
0 MANA DRAIN~
Syntax: cast 'mana drain' <victim>

By use of this spell, the caster can drain mana from his
victim.

Learned by:
Cleric (22)

~
0 CHARACTER TRADE~
Character trades are now allowed on Redemption.  Such exchanges must be
between characters of equivalent level, and with approximately the same
sophistication of equipment and number of abilities.  Whether a trade is
considered 'fair' or not is to be negotiated between the two parties
involved, and the Immortal doing the trade.  All trades must be approved and
performed by a 58+.  Both affected characters will lose 10 hp/mana/movement.
The characters will be renamed, and it is up to one of the new characters to
post a note stating both the old and new character names to everyone.
Note: All claimed equipment will not be adjusted to reflect the new
names.  This means all claimed equipment will be lootable; and this is also
considered a penalty for trading.

~
0 ACID BREATH~
Syntax: breath

All dragons have a natural affinity for the elements and have the ability to
expel it from their mouth in a powerful attack. Black dragons have the ability
to use their breath to spit acid at their opponent. This deals extensive damage
to their target and can destroy susceptible armors and increase their target's
AC. 

Learned by:
Black Dragons

~
0 FIRE BREATH~
Syntax: breath

All dragons have a natural affinity for the elements and have the ability to
expel it from their mouth in a powerful attack. Red dragons are able to breath
a torrent of flame over the entire room. The ashes from their flames can, for a
short time, blind those who have been struck by them. The heat of the flames
will often cause potions to boil and evaporate and burn other items beyond
recognition.

Learned by:
Red Dragons

~
0 FROST BREATH~
Syntax: breath

All dragons have a natural affinity for the elements and have the ability to
expel it from their mouth in a powerful attack. White dragons have the ability
to breathe out a chilling cone of frost over the entire room. The cold can
freeze and shatter potions as well as weakening those who are affected.

Learned by:
White Dragons

~
0 GAS BREATH~
Syntax: breath

All dragons have a natural affinity for the elements and have the ability to
expel it from their mouth in a powerful attack. Green dragons are full of toxic
gasses that they can blast out and fill an entire room. This gas can ve very
poisonous to those who breathe in its vapours.

Learned by:
Green Dragons

~
0 LIGHTNING BREATH~
Syntax: breath

All dragons have a natural affinity for the elements and have the ability to
expel it from their mouth in a powerful attack. Blue dragons can launch a
powerful bolt of lightning from their jaws. This is the most damaging of the
dragon breaths and can warp and melt some metal equipment.

Learned by:
Blue Dragons

~
0 SHOW~
This command is used to toggle the display of all the spells affecting your
character in your shore. When activated your affects list will be included when
you use the score or or oldscore commands. At low levels, only the spell name
will be displayed. At higher levels, the effects and duration of the spell will
also be shown.

(See also: 'help AFFECTS' 'help SCORE' 'help OLDSCORE')

~
0 AREA ZONE CONTROL~
Some areas within this world can be claimed and controlled by your guild
or clan.  Having control of an area will show up on 'where,' and will grant
your clan or guild extra regeneration and bonus damage while within that
area.
Each area is different; how you can gain control changes.  Sometimes
it may be as easy as killing a key mob, other times it may involve
a complicated quest.  In some areas, there may also be additional
bonuses or disadvantages for controlling the area.
{uCurrent list of areas:{x
Gingerbread House
Time (casts free haste)
Haon Dor (trees give away location of all but control clan)
High Tower (casts free Aurora)
Bosco's Breach (control clan gets to cross for free and collect tolls  on demand)
Sherwood Forest
Atlantis - Grants free entry to city and waterbreathing

~
0 ZANSHIN~
Monk, through vigorous training in the ways of combat, may find that they
can rejuvenate themselves even while under heavy stress.  Using the ancient
technique of Zanshin, monks regenerate at a rapid rate while in combat.

Learned by: Monk (42)

~
58 IMMGAIN GAIN SKILL SPELL~
Mortals may quest to gain extra abilities.  This is at a cost in QP per
CP.  The formula is as follows:
Below 500 hours:  2.5kQP/CP
Between 500-1500 hours: Cost reduces by 0.1kQP/CP per 100 hours.
            This cost reduces in steps, not linearly.
Above 1500 hours:  1.5kQP/CP
Also note: This formula is to remain secret.  You must always
check their hours and give them the cost for a given skill,
never explain how it works.

~
1 STATS RACESTATS STATISTICS STR DEX INT WIS CON~
Dragon:      Str 25 Dex 25 Int 25 Wis 25 Con 25
Dwarf:       Str 24 Dex 20 Int 20 Wis 23 Con 25
Elf:         Str 21 Dex 25 Int 24 Wis 23 Con 19
Gargoyle:    Str 25 Dex 22 Int 23 Wis 25 Con 22
Giant:       Str 25 Dex 21 Int 19 Wis 22 Con 25
Human:       Str 23 Dex 23 Int 23 Wis 23 Con 23
Kirre:       Str 23 Dex 24 Int 25 Wis 21 Con 24
Marid:       Str 19 Dex 22 Int 23 Wis 25 Con 25
Sliver:      Str 25 Dex 25 Int 25 Wis 25 Con 25
Troll:       Str 24 Dex 22 Int 21 Wis 22 Con 24
These are the maximum stats for each class.  They do not reflect
any bonuses which might be affected by you particular class.

~
58 DOUBLE PDOUBLE XP QP~
double status
double xp <ticks>
double qp <ticks>
pdouble xp 1     -- turn permanent double xp on
pdouble xp       -- turn permanent double xp off
pdouble qp 1     -- turn permanent double qp on
pdouble qp       -- turn permanent double qp off
This command will temporarily turn on double experience or double quest
points.  You can use 'double status' to see how many ticks remain until
the double runs out.  A reboot or crash will also reset the timer.
When it ends, morts will receive a message.
To turn double exp or qp on for extended durations, use 'pdouble'.
pdouble will turn it on persistently until it is turned off by
another pdouble command.  Pdouble lasts through reboot.
This command is level 58+

~
54 WELCOME~
welcome show
welcome send
welcome set <message>
The welcome command allows an immortal to work with the automatic message
which is displayed upon login.  If an immortal is wizi or incog, their
message will not be displayed to those below the threshold level.
Use 'welcome send' to send out your welcome message.  This is useful if you
logged in wizi and now want to reveal yourself manually.

~
54 GOODBYE~
goodbye show
goodbye send
goodbye set <message>
The goodbye command allows an immortal to work with the automatic message
which is displayed upon logout.  If an immortal is wizi or incog, their
message will not be displayed to those below the threshold level.
Use 'goodbye send' to send out your goodbye message.  This is useful if you
logged in wizi and now want to reveal yourself manually.

~
56 OCLONE MCLONE~
Syntax:   mclone <mobile>

{x          oclone <object>
{x
The mclone and oclone commands are shortcuts for clone mob and clone object,
respectively. They function in exactly the same way: for example, oclone
20*diamond will create 20 diamonds + 1 for the original.

~
56 OSTRING CSTRING~
Syntax:   cstring <character>

{x          ostring <object>
{x
The cstring and ostring commands are shortcuts for string char and string
object, respectively. They function in exactly the same way.

~
56 FINGER~
Syntax:   finger <character>

{x
The finger command can be used on offline characters to see how much time
has elapsed since their last logon. It will not work on currently
connected or ploaded characters.

~
56 CEDIT CLANEDIT~
Clanedit is the main command to edit or manipulate clans.
Syntax:

clanedit show (shows all clan basics)
clanedit show <clan> (shows a specific clan's data)
clanedit create <name> (create a new clan from scratch)
clanedit delete <name> (delete an existing clan)
clanedit name <clan> <name> (rename a clan's keyword)
clanedit whoname <clan> <whodesc> (rename a clan's who info)
clanedit leader <clan> <person> (set a player as leader of a clan)
clanedit leader <clan> none (wipe a clan's leader, player must be online)
clanedit r1|r2 <clan> <player>|none (set or remove a clan's recruiters)
clanedit vnum <clan> <number> (sets a clan's virtual num - should all be unique)
clanedit spawnterra <clan> <vnum> (sets a clan's terra repop when they die)
clanedit spawndom <clan> <vnum> (as above, but for dominia)
clanedit clanspell <clan> <skill/spell> (set a clan's clanspell)
clanedit spellcost <clan> <num> (cost of the clanspell, in DP)
clanedit loner <clan>, clanedit clanner <clan> (toggles loner and clanner status)

~
58 CLANINFO~
Syntax: claninfo

This command displays to a player the various clans in the game,
as well as their leaders.

~
0 DIAMOND PLATINUM DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Diamond dragons are the pinnacle of divine power  -  channels of pure sunlight
willing to sacrifice themselves for others. They can unleash a 'nova' burst
of radiant energy at all foes, and with 'defiance' become immune to sleep,
charm, and domination magic.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  nova        - Releases a burst of blinding radiant energy at all foes
  defiance    - Grants immunity to sleep, charm, and domination effects

~
1 ADAMANTITE PLATINUM DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Adamantite dragons are powerful combatants with scales as hard as the metal
they're named for. They can cast 'dullness' to blunt the effectiveness of an
enemy's weapons, and 'judgement' to deliver a powerful divine strike.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  dullness    - Reduces the damage output of an enemy's weapons
  judgement    - Delivers a powerful divine strike against a target

~
0 AMBER GOLD DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Amber dragons are wind-wielders who can trap foes and command the air around
them. They can 'encase' an enemy in hardened material to immobilize them,
and call up a devastating 'gale' to blast everything in the room.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  encase      - Encases a target, immobilizing them
  gale        - Blasts all foes in the room with a powerful wind

~
0 GALE~
Syntax: gale

Amber and Mithril dragons can beat their wings in a furious surge to conjure
a powerful gale, blasting every enemy in the room with wind damage. Targets
who fail to brace against the force are hurled into the air and dazed.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Amber Dragon (remort only)
Mithril Dragon (remort only)

~
0 SHEAR~
Syntax: shear <target>

Mithril dragons can launch a razor-thin blade of compressed wind at a target,
dealing wind damage. Shear has an extended reach - it can strike targets up
to two rooms away through open exits, though damage is reduced at greater
distance. Targets who fail to resist have their defenses stripped by the
wind_effect.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Mithril Dragon (remort only)

~
0 CYCLONE~
Syntax: cyclone

Mithril dragons can unleash a raging cyclone that batters every enemy in the
room with wind damage and strips their defenses. Targets who fail a strength
check against the force are swept out of the room through a random exit and
have their combat stopped. Sentinel mobs cannot be dislodged.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Mithril Dragon (remort only)

~
0 MITHRIL GOLD DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Mithril dragons are relentless wind warriors who can strip armor and
devastate groups. They can 'shear' a foe's defenses away, and call up a
'cyclone' to batter everything in the room.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  shear       - Strips away a target's defensive capabilities
  cyclone     - Batters all foes in the room with a violent whirlwind

~
0 CRYSTAL SILVER DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Crystal dragons live most of their lives beneath the ocean surface. They
permanently gain the ability to walk on water and breathe underwater. While
in a flooded or underwater room, they can use 'absorption' to inhale the
water around them and restore a spent breath weapon charge.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack    - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  absorption     - Restores a spent breath charge when used underwater
  water walk     - Permanent ability to walk on water (passive)
  water breathing- Permanent ability to breathe underwater (passive)

~
0 MERCURY SILVER DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Mercury dragons are the fastest of all dragon varieties - quick, merciless,
and fiercely protective. They can cast 'reduce' on themselves to shrink their
profile, making them considerably harder to hit in combat. Their speed is so
extreme that their bodies passively generate a quicksilver aura, granting
bursts of supernatural dexterity and attack speed.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack  - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  reduce       - Shrinks the dragon, reducing their size and making them harder to hit
  quicksilver  - Passive speed aura granting +DEX and extra attacks (automatic)

~
0 BRONZE COPPER DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies.  They are now  
able to use their tails in attacks.  Their scales have hardened on their  
hands, feet, and legs making it unnecessary to wear equipment any  
longer on those areas.  This ups their natural AC and DAM rates. 
Bronze dragons spend most of their days basking in the desert sun. They are
fierce and powerful warriors, able to emit a 'battle roar' that encourages their
friends to fight better. They are also used to living in the very sands of the
desert, and can 'burrow' underground anywhere outdoors in order to hide
themselves from their enemies.

~
0 JADE COPPER DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Jade dragons are mysterious and elusive. They can invoke the 'jade mantle'
to call up an orbiting jade stone shield that absorbs incoming damage, and
use 'stoneguard' to passively improve their parry in combat.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack  - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  jade mantle  - Orbiting jade shield that absorbs 40% of incoming damage
  stoneguard   - Passively boosts parry chance in combat

~
0 'JADE MANTLE'~
Syntax: cast 'jade mantle'

Jade dragons can call upon the earth to raise a slab of jade stone that
orbits them like a shield. The mantle absorbs 40% of all incoming damage
until its absorption pool is exhausted. Once the pool runs out the mantle
crumbles, and the earth needs a short time to reform before it can be
summoned again.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Jade Dragon (remort only)

~
0 STONEGUARD~
Syntax: none (passive)

Jade dragons develop an innate affinity for stone, which hardens their
natural defenses in combat. Each time the dragon is attacked there is a
chance for stoneguard to trigger, boosting their parry chance for that
exchange.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Jade Dragon (remort only)

~
0 OBSIDIAN IRON DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Obsidian dragons are found near volcanic craters, comfortable in both fire
and earth. They can use 'consume' to devour magical effects around them,
and can coat a weapon with obsidian shards using 'edge' to greatly enhance
its damage - at the cost of the weapon's longevity.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  consume     - Devours magical effects in the room
  edge        - Coats a weapon in obsidian to greatly increase damage temporarily

~
0 STEEL IRON DRAGON REMORT~
All dragon remorts have a better affinity with their bodies. They gain the
ability to use their tails in attacks, and their scales harden on the hands,
feet, and legs, improving their natural AC and damage rates.

Steel dragons are defensive powerhouses, wrapping themselves in shadow to
outlast any foe. They can cast 'umbral shell' to encase themselves in a
protective shroud of shadow energy, and 'umbral resilience' to further
strengthen their resistance to damage.

Skills/Spells gained:
  tail attack      - An additional natural weapon attack each round
  umbral shell     - Encases the dragon in a shroud of shadow energy for protection
  umbral resilience- Further strengthens the dragon's resistance to incoming damage

~
0 'UMBRAL SHELL' UMBRALSHELL~
Syntax: umbralshell

Steel dragons can draw upon the void to encase themselves in a hardened shell
of shadow energy. While the umbral shell is active, the crackling void
surrounding the dragon retaliates against attackers, releasing bursts of
shadow energy when struck.

Activating the shell costs mana and movement. The shell lasts for a short
time, but can be dismissed early by typing umbralshell again. While active,
the weight of the void slows the dragon's movement slightly.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Steel Dragon (remort only)

~
0 'UMBRAL RESILIENCE'~
Steel dragons are infused with void energy that builds as they endure damage
in combat. Each time they are struck, there is a chance for shadow energy to
accumulate within them, providing increasing damage reduction. As the energy
intensifies, it erupts outward in pulses of void, dealing shadow damage back
to the attacker.

This is a passive skill that activates automatically in combat. The shadow
energy dissipates naturally between fights.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Steel Dragon (remort only)

~
0 BRILLIANCE~
Syntax: c 'brilliance'

Platinum dragons have long since been known for their abilities to draw power
from the very sun itself. Brilliance allows them to imbue their own scales
with light, creating a radiant glow that enhances all of their physical
and mental abilities for a time.

~
0 DOMINATE~
Syntax: c 'dominate' <target>

Gold dragons are highly skilled in mental manipulation and telepathic magic.

They are able to temporarily cause prey to follow and serve them, even if
they do not know any kind of enchanting magic themselves. The domination
does not last a long while but it can be quite handy and useful in certain
circumstances.

~
0 "AURA OF PEACE"~
Syntax: c 'aura of peace'

Silver dragons are known for their gentle nature, and their disdain of fighting.

Why go into potentially dangerous combat when spells can do their work for you?

They have the ability to cause an 'aura of peace' in a room, which causes those
fighting in the room affected by it to periodically hesitate their attacks.

All silver dragons, however, are completely immune to the effect.

~
0 HIBERNATE~
Syntax: 'hibernate'

Copper dragons are one of the laziest breeds of dragons, and spend quite a lot
of their time burrowed under the desert sands sleeping. They are able to use
this laziness into something useful, however; when a copper dragon is done
hibernating, their bodies are completely healed. However, if interrupted in
the hibernation process their bodies will take serious damage.

~
0 HARDEN~
Syntax: harden

Iron dragons are by far the toughest of all dragons, able to withstand great
amounts of damage before succumbing to their injuries. All iron dragons are able
to supernaturally harden their scales through sheer concentration, making them
thicker and heavier. This enables them to greatly increase their defensive
abilities at the cost of agility.

~
0 NOVA~
Syntax: nova (use three times to detonate)

Diamond dragons channel the energy of the sun, building a charge across three
uses of nova. Each use requires a skill check to advance the charge. On the
third successful charge, the dragon detonates in a massive burst of divine
energy, dealing heavy damage to all targets in the room. The dragon takes
half damage from their own nova. The detonation also sends a tremor through
the entire area.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Diamond Dragon (remort only)

~
0 DEFIANCE~
Syntax: none (passive)

Diamond dragons radiate an aura of divine authority that protects them in
several ways. When struck by charm-type magic, there is a chance the effect
is negated entirely. Mobs scanning for targets may pass over the diamond
dragon entirely. Guards attempting to apprehend a diamond dragon for crimes
are cowed by its divine radiance and turn away.

All effects scale with skill level.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Diamond Dragon (remort only)

~
0 DULLNESS~
Syntax: none (automatic)

Adamantite dragons have some of the hardest scales known to the world. They are
so hard, in fact, that opponents who attack the adamantite can have their
weapons (or claws) severely blunted by the impact. Those who remain in combat
for long periods of time will find themselves automatically drained of attack
ability the longer they stay fighting the adamantite dragon.

Learned by:
Adamantite Platinum Dragon (remort only)

~
0 JUDGEMENT~
Syntax: judgement <target>

        judgement
Adamantite dragons can call down divine judgement upon a target, marking them
for 6 rounds. While the mark lasts, every hit the target receives has a
chance to trigger an additional divine effect - either piercing through their
damage reduction or empowering the strike with bonus divine force.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Adamantite Dragon (remort only)

~
0 PRESERVE~
Syntax: c 'preserve' <item>

Amber dragons have studied and mastered the arts of time itself, and the effects
that time has on objects and creatures. By using their renowned 'preserve'
spell, an amber dragon can keep an item that would normally rot or crumble and
cause its destruction to be vastly delayed. While this cannot freeze a food
item like cryogenesis, it works also on non-food items such as clan hall keys
or runist's tattoos.

Learned by:
Amber Dragon (remort only)

~
0 FREEDOM~
Syntax: none (automatic)

The adamantite dragon uses its reflective scales as a sort of energy battery,
allowing them to absorb the light of the sun and use that energy in place of
regular mana. This allows them via the 'freedom' ability to cast spells
without any sort of cost whatsoever from time to time.

~
0 MINDLEECH~
Syntax: mindleech

Amber dragons are renowned for their mental and cognitive powers. They are able
to emit a wave of powerful psychic energy, causing nearby friends and foes to
be drained of mana which is then absorbed by the amber dragon. This is
considered an aggressive action only to those not currently in the dragon's
group.

Learned by:
Amber Dragon (remort only)

~
0 IMBUE~
Syntax: c 'imbue' <item>

Mithril dragons are near-legendary for their abilities to enhance any item with
powerful magic. In the far past they were known for their abilities to create
true artifacts, but some of this skill still exists in their Imbue spell. This
spell enables them to enhance items, but at a cost - there is a chance the item
will be unable to hold the magic and will instead explode dramatically.

~
0 WINGBLAST~
Syntax: wingblast

The mithril dragon has a larger set of wings than any other dragon variety.

Though the biological reason for this is unknown, it certainly gives them
an advantage in combat. Any mithril dragon can buffet an area with their large
wings, causing debris and dust to swirl around and strike any in the immediate
vicinity, blinding and damaging them.

~
0 ABSORPTION~
Syntax: absorption

Crystal Silver Dragons permanently gain the ability to breathe underwater
and walk on water. While in a flooded or underwater room, they may use
'absorption' to inhale the surrounding water, which has a chance of
restoring one spent breath weapon charge.

Learned by:
Crystal Silver Dragon

~
0 QUICKSILVER~
Syntax: none (passive)

Mercury dragons move at supernatural speed. Each heartbeat tick, if not
already hasted, slowed, or quicksilvered, a Mercury dragon has a 50% chance
to enter the quicksilver state - a passive burst of speed that grants +4
dexterity and an extra attack each round.

The aura fades on its own and can be stripped by slow effects or an
opponent's 'quicken' skill.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Mercury Dragon (remort only)

~
0 REDUCE~
Syntax: c 'reduce'

In order to move even faster, mercury dragons have learned the art of shrinking
their very bodies. They learned this by reverse-engineering the dwarven art
of enlargement, and then using it for their own ends. A reduced mercury dragon
has all the benefits of being a dragon yet with the added bonuses of being
a small creature, such as a reduction in bash effectiveness, better hide, and
faster attack speed.

~
0 BURROW~
Syntax: burrow

Bronze dragons are one of the laziest of all dragon breeds. They spend much of
their time burrowed under the earth, snoozing away their lives. However, this
skill can certainly come in handy at times. By burrowing, a bronze dragon
can almost completely hide themselves from any foe, though it can only be
done outdoors.

~
0 'BATTLE ROAR'~
Syntax: battleroar

Bronze dragons, like all coppers, have a mighty set of lungs on them, and spend
a lot of their time calling to each other across the dunes, talking with
people, or even singing. Bronze dragons are a more irascible lot compared to
the other varieties, though, and spend much of their time in combat. They can
use their powerful battle roar to imbue their friends with the courage and
strength needed in a swirling melee.

~
0 'MYSTIC STONE'~
Syntax: c 'mystic stone'

The mysterious jade dragons hold secrets that few other races, dragons or not,
know about. One of these is the secret of the jade crystals that they carry
about on their person. These floating stones hold considerable power, though
a jade dragon can only use one of them at a time, and must wait for their
previous one to crumble before casting another.

Learned by:
Jade Dragon (remort only)

~
0 SHINAI~
Syntax: none (automatic)

Jade dragons are specially learned from birth in the lost art of Shinai, which
means 'the art of the parry'. They are so skilled at turning aside the weapons
of their foes that they are near-legendary at it. Shinai grants them a decent
bonus to all parrying attempts.

~
0 FLAMEGUARD~
Syntax: c 'flameguard' <item>

Obsidian dragons spend much of their time lounging about near volcanos. They
have studied these phenomena considerably and thus are able to use this
knowledge for something useful - the flameguard. A flameguarded item is
completely and permanently impervious to destruction by fire or lightning, and
grants an increased armor protection ability. However, maintaining this aura
of fire protection is costly, and the item drains a portion of mana from the
wearer while it is being worn.

~
0 EDGE~
Syntax: cast 'edge' <weapon>

The obsidian dragon can fragment pieces of their scales and coat a weapon
with obsidian shards. These shards are extremely sharp, enabling the weapon
to deal significantly more damage and attack faster than normal. Once edged,
only obsidian dragons may use the weapon. Ranged weapons cannot be edged.

This skill is for reclasses only.

Learned by:
Obsidian Dragon (remort only)

~
0 'IRON GUARD'~
syntax: ironguard
Steel dragons are near-legendary in their defensive capabilities.  By
focusing their mind on their scales, they are able to harden them to extreme
lengths, raising their defensive powers to heights undreamt of by other
races but at the cost of their scale's weight - it increases so much and
drags them down so heavily that they are barely able to walk from room to
room.

~
0 RAZORSCALES~
Syntax: none (automatic)

The scales of steel dragons are much sharper and more vicious than other dragon
varieties. Though this makes intimacy among their species somewhat more
dangerous, it also means that, in combat, they can deal serious amounts of
damage the longer their foe remains fighting them.

~
0 'DRAGON KICK'~
Syntax: dragon <target>

Aka 'The Art of Whirling Fire'
The art of the dragon kick is a legendary one, going back millenia. The monks
were able to study from the fire breathing red dragons, contemplating how the
initial blast of flames was more damaging than the heat itself. Thus they
worked to imitate that force and use it as a weapon of the body rather than
one of biology. Soon they developed the fearsome dragon kick, able to strike
in a flurry of kicks so fast that it burns the very air around them. Dragon
kicks can also stun the monk's victims.

~
0 'EAGLE CLAW'~
Syntax: eagle <victim>

Aka 'The Art of The Striking Crane'
For many centuries different monk groups have studied hard on how to improve
their basic attack methods. Mere punches and kicks are fine, but to penetrate
the tougher defense of larger and more armored foes they've needed to come up
with more efficient attacks. Thus was created the 'eagle claw' attack, able to
strike with the hands rapidly against a foe, hard enough that the sheer force
of it can blast armor aside and allow subsequent attacks to hit more vulnerable
areas.

Learned by:
Monk (automatic)

~
0 ENCASE~
Syntax: encase <target>

The amber dragon can exhale a torrent of viscous amber resin to immobilize
a foe. If the target fails to resist (STR save), they are sealed in
hardened amber and cannot move for 1-2 ticks. Costs 30 mana.

Learned by:
Amber Dragon (remort only)

~
0 'DEMON FIST'~
Syntax: demon <victim>

Aka 'The Art of the Horned Soul'
Far beyond any basic maneuvers, the demon fist is a punch that's evolved over
the centuries into something surpassing even life itself. The punch calls upon
the monk's chi, infusing the single attack with negative energy and blasting it
into the victim in the process. This functions similar to a curse spell, causing
the victim's particular deity to ignore them for a short while when they attempt
to recall out of a situation.

Plus, it really really hurts.

Learned by:
Monk (level 32)

~
0 'SHADOW WALK'~
Syntax: shadowwalk

Aka 'The Art of the Ghost'
The ninja is a master of stealth and quick movement. Able to move from place to
place with barely a whisper, ninjas have long since mastered the art of quick
mobility. Striking hard at their foe and then quickly departing is a very
useful survival skill. When shadow-walking, a ninja moves between rooms much
faster than any ordinary mortal can hope to move.

~
0 SMOKEBOMB~
Syntax: smokebomb

This ability enables a thief to fling a special ball filled with
smoke, ash, and dust at their feet, making their foes blinded
temporarily similar to kicking dirt at them.

Learned by:
Thief (18)

~
0 METALLIC DRAGON DRAGONCHANGE~
Syntax: dragonchange

        dragonchange confirm
Chromatic dragons who have matured (level 10+) and have not yet remoorted
or reclassed may undergo a permanent transformation into their metallic
counterpart. Visit a trainer and type dragonchange, then dragonchange
confirm to complete the process.

Chromatic to metallic conversions:
  Red    -> Gold
  Blue   -> Platinum
  White  -> Silver
  Green  -> Copper
  Black  -> Iron
This change is permanent and cannot be undone by unremort. Dragons who
have already remoorted, reclassed, or who are already metallic cannot
use this command.

(See also: help 'train dragon', help 'elemental wheel')

~
0 'ELEMENTAL WHEEL' ELEMENTS~
Dragons are divided into chromatic and metallic forms, each associated with
a distinct element. These elements determine the nature of their breath and
claw attacks, as well as their resistances and vulnerabilities.

CHROMATIC DRAGON ELEMENTS
  Fire      - Red Dragon
  Lightning - Blue Dragon
  Cold/Ice  - White Dragon
  Poison    - Green Dragon
  Acid      - Black Dragon
Chromatic dragons may undergo a permanent transformation into their metallic
counterpart via dragonchange. When they do, their element shifts to the
corresponding metallic element on the wheel.

METALLIC DRAGON ELEMENTS AND THE WHEEL
  Wind      - Gold Dragon         (from Red)
  Divine    - Platinum Dragon     (from Blue)
  Water     - Silver Dragon       (from White)
  Earth     - Copper Dragon       (from Green)
  Shadow    - Iron / Steel Dragon (from Black)

The five metallic elements form the elemental wheel, which governs their
resistances and vulnerabilities:

  Divine and Shadow are direct opposites - each strong against the other
  and vulnerable in return.

  Wind, Earth, and Water form a cycle:
    Wind beats Earth, Earth beats Water, Water beats Wind.

Each metallic dragon is resistant to their own element and vulnerable to the
element that counters them on the wheel.

(See also: help METALLIC DRAGON, help DRAGONCHANGE)

~
0 STUDY OFFLINE LEARNING~
Syntax:  study <primary/secondary> <skill or spell>

By dedicating yourself to continual learning, you may spend 
your time adventuring in intense study, practicing your skills
and improving them slowly.

You may begin studying at level 13.

~
0 FORGE~
Syntax: forge <material> <item>

This skill allows a battlesmith to create fully-functional equipment
using a block of material. The material must be held in the
hand and the skill can only be used in a workshop.
Possible items are:
collar chestplate helm greaves boots gloves armbands shield platemail
girth bracer

~
1 GRAFT ITEM~
Syntax: graft <weapon>, ungraft

This ability allows a battlesmith to force a weapon to attach to one of their wrists.

Though extremely painful, the benefits of doing so are numerous, such as being
unable to be disarmed.

~
1 CREATE FORGE~
Syntax: createforge

This ability allows a battlesmith to create a temporary workshop in any
location. It cannot be used in clan halls, however. Anything that would
normally require a workshop can be done in a temporary one, such as
crafting or building golems.

~
0 BLEEDER ARROW~
syntax:   bleeder <victim>
Rangers are effective marksmen.  Using their skills, they can
intentionally graze their opponents with ranged attack, causing massive
bleeding, but little actual damage.  The victim will bleed out health,
slowly losing hit points, and if the victim walks around, they will leave a
blood trail behind.  With some luck, that blood trail can lead the ranger to
their prey.
This action can be performed faster out of combat, but at a higher cost.

Learned by:
Rangers

~
0 PINDOWN PIN DOWN ARROW~
Syntax:  pindown <target>

Rangers are excellent marksman.  Taking careful aim, they can hit a
critical joint on their opponent.  In standard combat, this will slow them
down.  If done out of combat, the ranger always shoots for a knee or foot,
causing the enemy to frequently collapse when running.
This command can be performed faster out of combat, but at a higher cost.

Learned by:
Rangers

~
0 HIDEOUT HERMIT~
Syntax: hideout

Hermits are known for living a solitary life.  By digging in and forming
a home for themselves, hermits can reap the advantages of choosing their own
turf.  While at their hideout, a hermit regens faster, hits harder, and
cannot be hunted or seen on 'where'.  A hermit can only have one hideout at
a time.  

Learned by:
Hermits

~
0 FLETCH ARROW HERMIT~
Syntax: fletch <ammo type>

Hermits have learned how to quickly fletch tree limbs into various types
of ammunition.  They can make arrows (bows), bolts (crossbows), and bullets
(typically dart launchers).  

Learned by:

Hermits

~
1 'CLOSE COMBAT'~
Monks can learn the art of close combat, allowing them to focus
on the things happening directly around them. With the aid of this
skill group, monks can use the following abilities:
dragon kick            a multiple layered kick fast as fire
eagle claw            a claw so fast it strikes like lightning
choke hold            a hold on the victim may drown them
shoulder throw        someone trying to bash you? Counter with this!
demon fist           a strong punch attack 

~
1 HARASS~
This skill allows the zealot to turn the tides of the battle
by making everyone in the room that is not grouped focus their
fighting on the zealot.  

 

~
1 REMNANT REMNANTS~
When the dragonwar ended and most of Terra was destroyed, the remnants of
Bosco's army still survived. Traveling together, they eventually made camp
on the western side of Terra and established a military base. That army is
now known as the Remnants.

HISTORY
The cleric Xerges wandered the land of Terra after the war, gradually
gathering more of Bosco's children until they settled and began rebuilding.
As time passed, Xerges grew tired and fatigued from years of battle and
passed leadership to a druid named Greyson. Under Greyson the clan grew
further, but much like his predecessor he too had seen too many battles.
He became reclusive, and at times the clan felt as though it had no leader.

From that absence, another cleric stepped forward and took the reins.
Greyson stepped down to an advisor role. For a time, it seemed almost
peaceful -- until rumblings of Selina's children banding together in the
west heralded the rise of a rival faction. Warden, they called themselves.

RULES
1. Attacking unfinished characters is not allowed. Unfinished characters on
   either continent are to be left alone.

2. Wardens must be expelled from Terra. They may pass through our continent
   only if assisting us or with explicit permission.

3. Assist all newbies and loners to the best of your ability.

4. Respect your clanmates.

5. Maximum of 2 charmies when attacking other players, except when
   defending a hall break in progress.

6. Members are responsible for any player corpses they create. Corpses
   must be returned to the player in person.

7. Looting of equipment is not allowed. Only the following may be taken:
   wands, staves, scrolls, throwing items, gems, gold, and bank notes.

8. Equipment retained via disarm, gravitate, swap, heat metal, detonate,
   etc. must be returned to the owner. A fee of up to 2000 gold per item
   is acceptable. Equipment belonging to Wardens may be held until they
   return to Dominia.

RECRUITMENT
Remnants welcome anyone who upholds the clan's honor. No fees or quests
are required to join. Contact the clan leader or a recruiter to apply. A
brief quiz of the clan rules may be given at time of request.

RANKS
  Peasant    - Upon acceptance into the clan
  Apprentice - Upon donation of 20,000 gold
  Serf       - Upon donation of 25,000 gold
  Viscount   - Upon donation of 30,000 gold
  Noble      - Upon donation of 40,000 gold
  Cardinal   - Upon donation of 100,000 gold and 2 crafted items
  Knight     - Upon donation of 125,000 gold and 2 crafted items
  Templar    - Upon donation of 150,000 gold and 2 crafted items
  Lord       - Reserved for leadership

~
1 WARDEN WARDENS~
The Wardens trace their origins to the followers of Selina who helped win
the great dragonwar through unity and the hivemind of the slivers who ruled
Dominia. When Bosco restored the continent of Terra and a new army began to
grow there, the wards of Selina grew fearful of another invasion. Determined
to protect Dominia from being overrun again, they banded together and took
the name Wardens.

Where the Remnants are the surviving force of Bosco's fallen army, the
Wardens stand as the defenders of Selina's lands. The two clans have been
at odds since their founding, each claiming rightful dominion over the
continent's future.

(See also: help remnants)

~
1 PROMISE WORSHIP MYENA~
Myena has a promise she's kept to help the races of Dominia.  By
worshiping Myena, each race that starts on Dominia gets different abilities
related to what that race does best.  Trolls get extra regen, Gargoyles do
extra damage, Slivers get double their remort bonus, and Kirre get bonus
hand to hand abilities.  

All other races get double their regen rates.

~
1 HATRED WORSHIP KALLANA~
Kallana has a strong hatred for races that are polar opposites of those
she favors.  By choosing to worship Kallana, you can channel this hatred for
a short period of time.  

The following races have a strong hatred towards another and will get bonus
damage when choosing to channel Kallana's hatred: 

Sliver / Dragon, Dwarf / Elf, Human / Gargoyle, Troll / Giant, Kirre / Marid.

~
1 BLINDSIDE ROGUE~
When a rogue is assisting an attack made by another character, the rogue
has a chance to do hit harder and faster than others. This skill has a small
chance to go through their targets defense as the rouge circles around the target.

~
1 DOUBLE QP DOUBLE XP QUEST~
Syntax: quest double xp OR quest double qp.  

While at the quest master or quest mistress, you can choose to purchase
double xp or double qp for the cost of 10, 000 gold for 100 ticks.  The
quest master will automatically take the gold off your person, and if you do
not have enough will check to see if you have a bank note to cover the cost
and deduct from there.  
Double timers do not stack.

~
59 RUTHLESS RUTH~

~
1 UNREMORT UNRECLASS~
It is said that somewhere deep at the bottom of an abyss lies a special
place where you can forsake your current remort or reclass, should you be
willing to give up a part of your soul to do so.  

Those who wish to do this action must first find the location where it must
be done.  From there, the location itself will tell you how to find the item
you may need to prove you are willing to give up a portion of your soul.  

Syntax: remort forsake OR reclass forsake 

~
